# Canonical Praxion baseline cross-model-review caller template — thin,
# SHA-pinned invoker of the public `reusable-cross-model-review.yml` hub (the
# review-gate peer of `reusable-ci-autofix.yml`).
#
# This is the installable shape for the cross-model review gate's caller,
# realized from the earlier commented-out placeholder stub. Wiring an
# automated /onboard-project install step for this template (fleet rollout)
# is a separate, not-yet-built concern — see this repo's own
# `.github/workflows/cross-model-review.yml` for how Praxion installs and
# dogfoods this shape today.
#
# Two placeholders are filled at install time:
#   {{PRAXION_HUB}} — the hub's owner/repo (francisco-perez-sorrosal/praxion).
#   {{HUB_SHA}}     — the hub's commit SHA, resolved at install time to a real
#     40-hex value — never left as an unresolved placeholder or a mutable
#     tag/branch; every other `uses:` in this ecosystem is SHA-pinned the same way.
#
# All per-repo tunables (`cross_model_gate`, `reviewer_family`,
# `on_unavailable`) live in `.github/autofix-policy.yml`, installed alongside
# this caller — this file stays thin in logic, explicit only in trigger and
# privilege. See that template's own `review:` block for the full schema.
#
# The gate decision (which branches/PRs get reviewed, given the policy) lives
# in the hub, not here — this caller's only job is to own the real
# `pull_request` trigger (the ordinary event, never the privileged
# fork-context variant), the inverted-privilege permissions ceiling
# (`pull-requests: write` + `contents: read` ONLY — never the fixer's
# `contents: write` set), and the explicit `CURSOR_API_KEY` mapping — never
# the blanket inherit-all shorthand.
#
# Praxion's own caller (`.github/workflows/cross-model-review.yml`) differs
# only in the `uses:` ref: a same-repo local
# `uses: ./.github/workflows/reusable-cross-model-review.yml` (tracks HEAD —
# correct for the repo that develops the hub), never a cross-repo SHA pin —
# the same deliberate divergence as `ci-autofix.yml.tmpl`'s own caller #1.
# Delete this comment after tailoring.

name: Cross-Model Review

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]

permissions: {}  # least-privilege; the job below grants only the inverted-privilege ceiling

jobs:
  review:
    permissions:                          # the load-bearing invariant — EXACTLY
                                           # these two grants, never the fixer's
                                           # contents:write/id-token:write set
      pull-requests: write
      contents: read
    uses: {{PRAXION_HUB}}/.github/workflows/reusable-cross-model-review.yml@{{HUB_SHA}}
    with:
      policy_path: .github/autofix-policy.yml
    secrets:
      CURSOR_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CURSOR_API_KEY }}
